      "page_title": "Hashes: Field-Level Objects",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "hash",
                "lines": [
                  "`HGET` one field",
                  "`HINCRBY` atomic",
                  "partial transfer",
                  "per-field TTL"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "JSON string",
                "lines": [
                  "read-parse-modify-write",
                  "full value on the wire",
                  "one round trip",
                  "nesting allowed"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Which one",
          "text": "JSON-in-a-string wins when you always read the whole object. A hash wins when fields are updated independently or read selectively."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Memory: The Sharding Trick"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "redis",
          "lines": [
            "# 1M flags as 1M top-level keys: ~80 MB overhead",
            "HSET bucket:10 0 1   # id 1000 -> 1000/100, 1000%100",
            "HSET bucket:10 1 0   # id 1001",
            "OBJECT ENCODING bucket:10   # listpack"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`listpack` while under 128 entries and 64-byte values",
            "`hashtable` above either threshold",
            "Every top-level key costs ~50–90 bytes before your data",
            "robj + dict entry + expire entry + key string",
            "Hashes amortize that overhead across all their fields"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Limits and mistakes",
          "items": [
            "Fields cannot nest; values are always strings",
            "No independent type beyond the field TTL",
            "`HGETALL` on a 100k-field bucket ships megabytes",
            "That one command stalls the event loop"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`HMSET` deprecated — variadic `HSET` replaces it",
            "`HINCRBY`/`HINCRBYFLOAT`: atomic per-field counters",
            "A whole stats object in one key, no read-modify-write race",
            "`HKEYS`/`HVALS`/`HGETALL` are all O(N) — use `HSCAN`",
            "`HRANDFIELD key [count] [WITHVALUES]` samples fields",
            "Negative count allows repeats, mirroring `SRANDMEMBER`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Per-field TTL",
          "text": "`HEXPIRE`/`HPEXPIRE`/`HEXPIREAT` expire one field without touching the rest of the object. `HTTL` reads it, `HPERSIST` removes it."
        }
      ]
    },
